{title: Better Than She}
{subtitle: Esther 1:1–5; 1:9; 1:10–11; 1:12; 1:13–20; 1:21–22}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 83}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
This happened in the days of Ahasuerus
Ruling [C]over a hundred and [Bb]twen-ty-sev-en [C]provinces
[Dm]Seated on his royal [C]throne in Susa
In the [Bb]third year of his [C]reign he [Am]gave a [Dm]feast
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
A hundred and eighty days of wealth displayed
Splendid [C]glory of his greatness [Bb]seen
[C]Then [Dm]seven days in the garden [C]court
For all the [Bb]people in the [C]cita[Dm]del
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Queen [Bb]Vashti gave a ban[C]quet for the [Dm]women
In the [C]royal palace of the [Bb]king
On the seventh day his [C]heart was [Dm]merry
With [Bb]wine he com[C]manded the [Dm]eunuchs
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Bring Queen [Bb]Vashti [C]wearing her [Dm]royal crown
To dis[C]play her beauty to the [Bb]peoples
She was lovely to [C]look at they [Dm]said
But she re[Bb]fused to [C]come at the com[Dm]mand
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The king became furious in his heart
[C]His anger burned within [Bb]him deep
He [Dm]consulted the wise men who [C]knew the law
To [Bb]ask what [C]should be done with [Dm]her
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]Memucan an[C]swered before the [Dm]king
She has [C]wronged all the of[Bb]ficials
The women will de[C]spise their [Dm]husbands
If she [Bb]does not o[C]bey the de[Dm]cree
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Let the [Bb]royal po[C]sition go to an[Dm]other
To a [Bb]woman who is [C]better than [Dm]she
{end_of_verse}
